  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ZnCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi></mover><mi>ZnO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Heating in absence of oxygen in calcination.</p><p>(B)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Zns</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ZnO</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>heating in presence of oxygen in roasting Hence (A)&nbsp;is calcination while (B) in roasting.</p>",
